  "id": "thinking-style",
  "term": "thinking style",
  "definition": "Thinking style is a person’s characteristic way of approaching information, such as a more holistic or more analytic mode of thought. In this research context, it refers to differences in how people handle contradictory information, with holistic thinkers tending to reconcile contradictions more readily than analytic thinkers.",
